 "notes": "The manuscript contains two dates and reigns: the main colophon dates to NS 135 (Caitra śukla 10, Thursday = danuja-ripu-gurau/guru-vāsara) during the joint/divided rule of Bhojadeva, Rudradeva, and Lakṣmīkāmadeva in Nepālamaṇḍala at Śrī-Lhaṃ-vihāra copied by Sujatabhadra (probably Sujātabhadra). A later addition in hooked Nepalese hand records a restoration/rescue of the manuscript in year 259 (śatasya dvitīye pañcāsatā parigate navamāñcitena = 259 NS) Kārtika śukla 5 under king Mānadeva (Mānadeva IV / Mānadeva of NS 259 / c. 1139 CE) by someone mentioning 'vajriṇa' (or a Vajrayāna practitioner).",
